r reserved for the enemies  that scared she was a child and for me  the sound of this one is still hugely  disconcerting Marie dad's might have a  semi stupid name but when they first  popped up in ocarina of time they proved  the bassam BS beasty with powers of  paralysis by any other name would be as  scary that persistent droning coupled  with a chilling scream when link gets  too close is a pretty solid memory for  kids that owned n64 not only that but if  you're in a tight vicinity the dudes  would paralyze you jump on your back and  bite at you while you mash the a and B  buttons trying to get away they're easy  enough to avoid but they're unnaturally  idle nature and drowning urns though a  place on this list number three on my  list was encountered Wells Arena and I  played through the ghost heavy fatal  frame - pretty much every encounter in  Fatal Frame 2 was totally terrifying but  as it happens not all horrifying ghosty  attacks are made equal some way into the  game whilst rummaging for shiny items  you encounter a room with a box  unluckily the box house a particularly  creepy ghost aptly named woman in box  her attack pattern consisted of  stumbling slowly toward the player with  her long hair pulled over like the girl  from the ring before revealing a freaky  face and launching full-speed for a  final grapple which unfortunately is  pretty much the only ton you can snap a  photo of her to deal a chunk of damage  my second-to-last pic also happens to  come from the Zelda series but I  maintain that it is a damn terrifying  universe with no monstrous creepy as  wall masters I took on a link between  worlds on 3ds recently and was  unfortunate enough to encounter these  bastards yet again the big C's are just  floating hands that threaten you with a  growing shadow of a link before swatting  you from above  they're also known to crawl along the  ground grab it link and do all the  things at hands do but in a gigantic  violent form frustratingly if they 